# build.env
#
# Where ./crossbuild.sh -d puts what it built. crossbuild.sh copies this file
# to build.env on its first run and stops so you can fill it in; build.env
# names one person's board, so it stays out of git.
#
# Every run reads it and every setting below needs a value, so a build says
# what is missing before it spends a minute compiling. The two that name your
# board in particular are commented out and have to be filled in; the rest
# carry a default that suits an appliance board.

# ssh destination of the board, as scp and ssh take it. The user name is also
# the web interface's, and ~/.qbone-pw holds that password.
#QUNILATOR_HOST=you@yourboard.local

# The bus the board's cape bridges: qbus (a QBone) or unibus (a UniBone). A
# build with no option builds for this, which is what makes a deploy land a
# binary the board can run; -u and -q override it for one run.
#QUNILATOR_BUS=qbus

# What is on the board:
#
#   appliance  a board flashed from the release image. The emulator is
#              /usr/bin/<name> - qbone or unibone, whichever bus the build is
#              for - and <name>.service runs it. The deploy replaces that file
#              and restarts the unit.
#
#   checkout   a board carrying a source tree, running the binary out of it.
#              The deploy replaces 10.03_app_demo/4_deploy_<suffix>/demo below
#              QUNILATOR_REMOTE_DIR.
QUNILATOR_DEPLOY_MODE=appliance

# checkout mode: the source tree on the board, relative to the login directory
# or absolute. Appliance mode does not deploy there, but the setting is still
# read, so leave the default rather than emptying it.
QUNILATOR_REMOTE_DIR=QUniLator

# appliance mode: also send the web frontend to /usr/share/qunilator/frontend.
# It is served from disk, so this takes effect without a restart. Needs a built
# bundle - 'npm ci && npm run build' in 10.05_web/3_frontend.
#QUNILATOR_DEPLOY_FRONTEND=1

# An appliance deploy writes below /usr and restarts a unit, so the account
# QUNILATOR_HOST names needs sudo there.
